WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.829
Welcome to Gabriel Archangel Investments.

2
00:00:05.429 --> 00:00:10.044
Here's how our system finds outstanding companies, ranks them objectively, and

3
00:00:10.044 --> 00:00:12.115
manages the risk of every position.

4
00:00:14.115 --> 00:00:15.530
Our starting point is simple.

5
00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:18.834
Market leaders often trade close to their all-time high:

6
00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:21.208
the highest price the stock has ever reached.

7
00:00:21.708 --> 00:00:26.011
So instead of chasing stocks that keep falling, we focus on quality companies

8
00:00:26.011 --> 00:00:27.799
the market is already rewarding.

9
00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:31.388
Step one: the universe.

10
00:00:31.838 --> 00:00:36.533
We begin with a curated list of thirty quality leaders from around the world,

11
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.741
across technology, healthcare, industry, consumer and financial data.

12
00:00:43.141 --> 00:00:45.127
Step two: fresh data, every night.

13
00:00:45.577 --> 00:00:50.162
An automated process collects prices, profitability, growth and balance-sheet

14
00:00:50.162 --> 00:00:54.390
figures for every company, and stores the results in a scores database.

15
00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:59.120
Prices refresh every fifteen minutes, fundamentals every day, and sales

16
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.252
history every week.

17
00:01:02.652 --> 00:01:04.217
Step three: the Cannon Score.

18
00:01:04.667 --> 00:01:09.140
Every company receives one clear number, from zero to one hundred, built from

19
00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:09.953
seven factors.

20
00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:14.269
Proximity to the all-time high is worth up to twenty-five points.

21
00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:19.168
Return on invested capital, or how efficiently the business turns money into

22
00:01:19.168 --> 00:01:20.066
profit: twenty.

23
00:01:20.416 --> 00:01:22.602
Sales growth over three years: twenty.

24
00:01:22.952 --> 00:01:26.810
Technical strength, the stock's performance over the last twelve months:

25
00:01:26.810 --> 00:01:27.239
fifteen.

26
00:01:27.589 --> 00:01:28.826
Net margin: ten.

27
00:01:29.176 --> 00:01:30.818
Balance-sheet strength: five.

28
00:01:31.168 --> 00:01:33.656
And trading volume and liquidity: five more.

29
00:01:36.256 --> 00:01:37.576
Let's look at an example.

30
00:01:38.076 --> 00:01:42.276
A company trading three percent below its high, earning thirty-five percent on

31
00:01:42.276 --> 00:01:46.207
its capital, growing sales twenty-two percent a year, and carrying little

32
00:01:46.207 --> 00:01:48.523
debt, scores eighty-two out of one hundred.

33
00:01:49.223 --> 00:01:53.475
Any company scoring sixty or more is highlighted as a top candidate on the

34
00:01:53.475 --> 00:01:54.050
dashboard.

35
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.261
Step four: screen and compare.

36
00:01:58.711 --> 00:02:03.250
Filters for distance to the high, return on capital, valuation, margins, debt

37
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:07.553
and trend narrow the list down to a handful of candidates worth studying.

38
00:02:10.153 --> 00:02:12.999
Step five, and the most important: how much to buy.

39
00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:16.355
First, we decide the most we are willing to lose.

40
00:02:16.355 --> 00:02:19.851
For example, one percent of a fifty-thousand-dollar account:

41
00:02:19.851 --> 00:02:21.075
five hundred dollars.

42
00:02:21.575 --> 00:02:25.619
If we buy at one hundred dollars and place a protective stop at ninety, we

43
00:02:25.619 --> 00:02:27.094
risk ten dollars per share.

44
00:02:27.594 --> 00:02:30.591
Five hundred divided by ten gives us fifty shares.

45
00:02:31.291 --> 00:02:35.435
If the price reaches the stop, we exit, and the loss is the five hundred

46
00:02:35.435 --> 00:02:39.751
dollars we planned. Profit targets are set at one, two and three times that

47
00:02:39.751 --> 00:02:40.039
risk.

48
00:02:40.639 --> 00:02:45.328
The system also adds up the risk of every open position, so total portfolio

49
00:02:45.328 --> 00:02:46.766
risk is always visible.

50
00:02:49.566 --> 00:02:50.757
So, in five steps:

51
00:02:51.057 --> 00:02:55.266
a quality universe, fresh data every night, an objective score, focused

52
00:02:55.266 --> 00:02:58.053
screening, and disciplined risk on every trade.

53
00:02:58.653 --> 00:03:01.415
That is how Gabriel Archangel Investments works.

54
00:03:03.615 --> 00:03:05.678
Follow the leaders. Respect the risk.
